To enter Vlad's tower, you need to go to the level immediately below the
bottom level of his tower.  There will be two up stairways, one of which
leads to his tower.  You may be having problems if an object or boulder
is obscuring the second stairway.  Make sure you're not confusing Vlad's
tower with the Wizard's tower.

To quote Robert DeLoura (deloura@noaapmel.gov),

> Vlad's Tower is 3 levels high.  (It goes up, not down.  Bottom is 'V1'.)
> Level V1 always has a Long Sword, a Lock Pick, an Elven Cloak, and a
>   Blindfold.  They're always on trapped spaces, as well.
> There's an Amulet of Life Saving on V2.  There is also an Amulet of
>   Strangulation, Water Walking Boots, a Crystal Plate Mail, and a Spellbook
>   of Invisibility.
> Vlad is on V3, with the Candelabrum of Invocation.

